Z||000009||Mach10||12-20-2001||03:53 PM||||I'd be worried about the block. The weak points are the block and the crank. The duke is a good economy engine, and has <I>good</I> power... But as a performance item... It doesn't have much going for it. That block will break like an egg at higher revs...<P>The ONLY thing I could think of would be to have the rotating assembly balanced. That will relieve stress, somewhat. But at 6000+ speeds... I'd be REALLY keen on a scatter sheild around the driver seats... Sorry  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||9
