Z||000020||jelly2m8||12-21-2001||03:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B> [QUOTE]I was refering to the block style. If I'm not mistaken, if the 4.3's already in there, then the MOUNTING CHANGES HAVE ALREADY BEEN MADE. I am under the impression that the 3800 and the 4.3L block are very similar, in terms of engine mount locations... By your logic, the GM 60* block will happily bolt in place of the 90*. Er... No. Again, I was refering to the BLOCK STYLE. Wasn't talking about the internals. Get your foot off my throat, or you're gonna LOSE IT &gt;:\<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Hang chilly Mach10 buddy. I wasn't out to flame you. Riceboyfiero was excited there because they had a 90* engine in there, and was wondering how they did that.<P> Maybe I should have posted this as a reply to his. My mistake.<P> The 60*, 90* series FWD engines use the same transmission bolt patten.<P> If I remember correctly, the 4.3L is a 90* setup, like the 3.0, 3.3, 3.8, and 3800 series motors. I do know that it is basically a 5.7L with 2 cylinders lopped off. Looking at the outside of the block, it looks very similiar to the SBC blocks. It uses the same transmission bolt pattern as the SBC also<P> The 90* 3.0, 3.3, 3.8, and 3800 series engine blocks look very different to me.<P><BR> Hope your throat is o.k.<P>Peace dude!<P> <P> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
